WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.150
After an uneven final season comprised of
only six episodes, fans were excited, concerned,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.960
and downright desperate to see how the Game
of Thrones saga would finally end.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.440
From the Iron Throne to the fate of Westeros
and the final showdown between Daenerys and

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.040
Jon Snow, here's what the ending of Game of
Thrones means not just for the final season,

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.780
but for the entire series.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.519
Beware: spoilers are coming!

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.319
After the burning of King's Landing in the
previous episode, several main characters

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:31.689
wander through the brutal aftermath, with
Tyrion Lannister, the Hand of the Queen, looking

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.620
stricken as he walks down ruined streets and
sees the bodies of those Daenerys burned without

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.140
mercy.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.960
As he and Jon Snow survey the destruction,
Jon and Tyrion separately set off to meet

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:42.580
the queen.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.640
Jon's journey finds him at odds with Grey
Worm over the execution of Lannister soldiers.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.660
But soon after Tyrion sets off on his own,
he makes a horrifying discovery.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.880
In a truly heartbreaking moment, Tyrion finds
the bodies of his brother and sister and breaks

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.940
down amid the rubble.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.980
With the rest of his house literally entombed,
Tyrion finds himself suddenly alone, and in

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.160
that moment, his resolve to defy his queen
strengthens.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:12.060
Later, as the Dothraki and Unsullied celebrate
their victory, Daenerys makes a grand entrance,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.680
riding atop Drogon and landing in a perfect
shot with her silhouetted by his wings.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.160
While she gives a full-throated victory speech
in which she praises her army for taking down

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.810
a tyrant and claiming the city as their own,
viewers know the truth: Dany is no better

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.780
than the tyrant she aims to replace.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.920
In fact, she's probably a lot worse, as she
announces her plans to prolong the war and

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.480
conquer the rest of the world.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.040
Daenerys has always bent towards justice,
but with this proclamation, it seems as if

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.200
she's finally gone too far, and even her most
trusted advisors seem frightened by her endless

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.320
hunger for power.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:50.259
In the aftermath of the siege on King's Landing,
during which Tyrion begged his queen to show

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:54.619
mercy to those who couldn't defend themselves,
it seems as if the last remaining Lannister

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:59.560
can no longer bring himself to follow Daenerys,
and has seen her for what she really is - or

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.740
at least what she's ultimately become.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:06.460
Daenerys is already furious with Tyrion after
finding out that he freed Jaime - which ultimately

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.940
doesn't even matter, considering that Jaime
and Cersei are both dead.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.360
But Tyrion has his own grievances with the
Mother of Dragons.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.320
As they confront each other atop a ruined
King's Landing, he admits that he freed his

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.720
brother, but reminds her that she decimated
an entire city.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.260
Moments later, he tosses aside the badge that
identifies him as Hand of the Queen.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.100
Daenerys immediately has him arrested, but
his point is made, marking yet another advisor

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.640
who leaves her side when she needs them the
most.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.830
Her transformation into a new version of her
father, the Mad King, who killed anyone who

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.540
displeased him, is complete.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.020
As Tyrion sits in captivity, awaiting his
certain execution, he's visited by a visibly

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:49.520
torn Jon Snow, who, despite his allegiance
to Daenerys, still obviously trusts Tyrion's

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.020
counsel.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.400
Jon defends Daenerys at first, saying that
though he can't condone what happened, the

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.460
war is finally over.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:00.140
But Tyrion persists, reminding Jon that Daenerys
isn't even close to finished, and the only

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:04.480
way she can achieve her ultimate goal is through
even more death and destruction on a global

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:04.980
scale.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.260
Tyrion also reminds Jon that he once had the
power to do what Daenerys did - specifically,

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.600
to ride atop a dragon and destroy an entire
city - and he never would.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.260
Before she sacked King's Landing, Daenerys'
destruction often seemed entirely righteous

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:23.020
- like when she freed slaves and killed their
masters - but as Tyrion points out, the murder

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.810
of countless innocent men, women, and children
can't possibly be defended, and at this point,

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.520
the Dragon Queen will stop at nothing to achieve
her goals.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.700
Though Tyrion recognizes that "love is more
powerful than reason," he still does everything

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.020
in his power to convince Jon of the path ahead:

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.760
"You've tried to protect people.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.280
Who is the greatest threat to the people now?"

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.280
Jon - the true heir to the throne, having
received wise counsel from the Hand - knows

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:53.940
that there's only one move left to finally
end the war once and for all.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.960
Jon finds Daenerys in the Throne Room, admiring
the throne she's worked so hard to win.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.420
As he asks her why she murdered children in
the streets of the capital, she tries to entice

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.720
him with her vision of the "new world" the
two of them can build together.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:10.620
As they embrace, Jon proclaims that Daenerys
will always be his queen.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:15.760
Just when it seems like all hope for peace
is lost, he stabs her, holding her and weeping.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.460
This is the moment the series has been building
toward since the beginning.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.080
Ned Stark lost his head for being too honorable.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.320
In the end, Jon Snow betrayed his honor in
order to save it.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.060
He made the impossible choice: killing his
lover and queen, to whom he'd pledged his

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.560
eternal loyalty, for the greater good of his
family and the world.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:39.940
After Jon becomes the Queenslayer, all is
silent for a moment, until Drogon reappears,

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.919
coming face to face with Jon in a frightening
moment when it seems like the last remaining

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.300
Targaryen might immediately face justice for
killing the Mother of Dragons.

00:04:48.409 --> 00:04:52.719
However, Drogon's anguish over the death of
his mother is directed not at Jon, but at

00:04:52.719 --> 00:04:58.080
something entirely different - specifically,
the Iron Throne, which he torches into a melted

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.240
pile of slag in a stream of fire.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:04.060
The ultimate symbol of power in Westeros is
completely destroyed.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:08.140
Daenerys has always referred to her dragons
as her "children," and her final moments with

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:13.100
Drogon are heartfelt, as he tries to nudge
her awake and screams in pain for his lost

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:13.600
mother.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:18.180
After demolishing the Throne once and for
all, Drogon gently lifts Daenerys off the

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:23.130
ground and flies away with her safely ensconced
in his claws, making for a fitting end to

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.020
Daenerys' arc.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:29.020
She was reborn with all three of her dragons,
and even in death, she remains a part of her

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.220
only remaining child.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.860
Moreover, Drogon identifies Dany's true killer
without uttering a word.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:37.740
It wasn't Jon who is responsible for the end
of her life.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.160
Instead, it was her unending quest to seek
the Iron Throne itself.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.920
It's like Cersei said way back in season one:

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.120
"When you play the game of thrones you win,
or you die.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.140
There is no middle ground.”

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.460
Since the beginning, the throne has represented
death.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:57.720
It was composed of the weapons of the king's
enemies, and men and women fought and killed

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.180
for a chance to sit on it.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.660
Daenerys always wanted to break the wheel.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.360
Now that Drogon has destroyed the Iron Throne,
the wheel in Westeros has finally been broken.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:11.300
Weeks after Daenerys' death, Tyrion is led
out of his cell to face a new council, made

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:15.620
up of familiar characters alongside a few
faces who have been absent from the show for

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.719
several seasons.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.620
The Unsullied have taken King's Landing and
are holding Jon and Tyrion captive, and Tyrion

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.720
must not only argue his case against Grey
Worm, but for the entire council.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.380
But before Tyrion's fate can be decided, the
lords and ladies of Westeros must choose a

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.180
new monarch.

00:06:31.469 --> 00:06:35.700
As the group debates who should rule next,
Tyrion is asked whether or not he wants the

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.200
job.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:40.940
He describes himself as the worst possible
choice, and no one really argues his points.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:45.979
In order to explain who he does have in mind,
however, Tyrion begins by telling the assembled

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:50.710
that what unites everybody is the power of
a story, then identifying the person he says

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:55.310
has the "best story" - Bran Stark, who has
journeyed beyond the Wall and back to become

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.180
the all-seeing Three-Eyed Raven.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:02.200
Everybody seems a bit stunned by this unexpected
nomination - except for Bran, but now that

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:05.480
he's the Three-Eyed Raven, looking surprised
isn't really his thing.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.860
But once Tyrion points out that because Bran
can't have children, the leader of Westeros

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:14.300
will be chosen rather than receive it by birthright,
he receives a unanimous vote.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:19.039
After everything the Starks have lived through,
the eldest surviving Stark son is named Bran

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.500
the Broken, First of His Name.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:25.780
In exchange, Bran chooses Tyrion as his new
Hand, bringing his arc to a fitting conclusion.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:30.500
As far as his own arc is concerned, Bran's
ascension to the throne may seem surprising

00:07:30.509 --> 00:07:33.150
given the path his story has taken throughout
the series.

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:38.159
Moreover, in this final season, Bran doesn't
actually do much, aside from glower at other

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:40.660
characters from his chair and say weird things.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:45.440
But if you remember the very first episode
of the series, Bran has a front-row seat to

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.440
an execution, carried out by his father.

00:07:47.849 --> 00:07:51.920
The scene is meant as a lesson for Bran in
the rules of justice and leadership: namely

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:54.560
that duty and honor justifies violence and
death.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:59.559
But now that Bran will take over as King of
Westeros in the wake of Daenerys's war crimes,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.900
it seems like a sure bet that he'll have taken
his father's lesson and will apply the inverse.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:09.100
Mercy, fairness, and justice trump duty and
honor, and are the only true path to peace

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:09.600
and life.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:14.400
Since the beginning of the season, Sansa,
who has established herself as a fair leader

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.840
as well as a sharp and shrewd strategist,
has bristled at the thought of the North falling

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:20.140
under anyone's rule.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:24.539
Throughout Daenerys' reign, she argued for
the North to maintain its status as an independent

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.120
territory with its own monarchs and wardens.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:31.159
When Jon told her about his true parentage,
she immediately shared the information with

00:08:31.159 --> 00:08:35.280
Tyrion, clearly hoping to keep control of
the North by not only keeping a tyrant from

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:38.780
taking the throne, but by putting a half-Stark
regent in power.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:43.300
While that plan didn't pan out, Sansa ultimately
made sure the North was taken care of.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:48.180
During the council meeting, Sansa is hesitant
to cast a vote in favor of Bran, and as she

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.120
turns to her brother and tells him that she
loves him and that she's sure he'll be a great

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:56.590
king, she insists that the North remain its
own territory, and Bran grants her request.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:01.340
Thanks to Sansa, the North can keep its identity
and its independence, and since the North

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.630
always remembers, its citizens will certainly
remember what the Lady of Winterfell did to

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:06.420
protect them.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.580
As for the rest of the characters, each of
them is seen off properly, with arcs completed,

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.500
stories told, and journeys finally finished.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:18.420
Grey Worm sets off for Naath alone, still
smarting after losing both Missandei and his

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:18.920
queen.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:24.680
Bronn returns to claim his lordship of Highgarden
and becomes Master of Coin in Bran's administration,

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:29.080
flanked by a small council that includes Brienne,
Davos, Sam, and Tyrion.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.980
Podrick Payne, now Bran's attendant, has been
knighted and made a member of the Kingsguard

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:35.360
since viewers last saw him.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:39.540
Not only are several stories completed, but
some characters write out stories of their

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.200
own, making sure the people they lost won't
be forgotten.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:46.840
After finding Jaime's unfinished entry in
the book listing Westerosi knights, Brienne

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:50.900
completes it herself, capping it off by writing,
"Died protecting his queen."

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:55.300
Meanwhile, Sam presents the council with a
book written by one of the Maesters called

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.040
- what else?

00:09:56.210 --> 00:10:00.600
- A Song of Ice and Fire, in an obvious and
rather heavy-handed reference to the book

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.360
series by George R.R. Martin on which the
series is based.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.720
Unlike Martin's series, however, this book
appears to be finished.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:12.640
Jon, for murdering the queen, is banished
back into the Night's Watch, a symbolic move,

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:17.000
and the only way the council can seem to broker
peace with the Unsullied and get them to relinquish

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.280
their hold on the city.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:23.440
Upon returning to Castle Black, Jon reunites
with Tormund as well as a large group of wildlings

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.270
and his direwolf Ghost, who, despite missing
an ear, is thrilled to see his master once

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:28.760
again.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:34.340
In the end, the series closes with shots of
the family with which it began - the Starks,

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:37.280
who have scattered to various corners of Westeros
and beyond.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:42.570
Sansa is coronated at Winterfell, proudly
taking her seat as the citizens of the North

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.320
raise their swords and cheer for the new Queen
in the North.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:49.900
Arya boards a ship headed for the unknown
lands west of Westeros, sailing under the

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:53.910
Stark banner on a quest to learn what lies
beyond the part of the world where their maps

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:54.400
end.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:58.940
Meanwhile, Jon sets out from Castle Black
with Tormund, Ghost, and a group of wildlings

00:10:58.940 --> 00:10:59.440
in tow.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:03.940
As they begin their journey to the far North,
some green growth can be seen peeking out

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:06.100
from underneath the thick layers of snow.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:11.000
Throughout Game of Thrones' run, audiences
have always been told that "winter is coming."

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:15.470
But now that the Night King is no more and
a new age has begun in Westeros, it seems

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.800
as if the show's long winter may finally be
coming to an end.

